commit.message:
apply grasp-server PR-kind default to ngit send

commit 9e06e7b added the GRASP-server heuristic to the git-remote-nostr
push path but missed the equivalent block in ngit send.  Mirror the same
three-variable pattern:

  let commits_too_big = ...;
  let has_submodules  = ...;
  let repo_has_grasp_server = !repo_ref.grasp_servers().is_empty();
  let should_be_pr = (existing PR) || commits_too_big || has_submodules
                   || (root_proposal.is_none() && repo_has_grasp_server);

also update the CHANGELOG entry to mention ngit send alongside git push
